# Loom Durable Agent Obligation

Concept-ID: `SOUNIO-DURABLE-AGENT-OBLIGATION`

Status: executable bounded witness for one durable local filesystem authority.

## Semantic Lane

```text
Semantic-Lane-ID: codex-loom-obligation-20260824
Owner: codex/session-01a02a17-f139-7613-98a1-
Concept-IDs: SOUNIO-DURABLE-AGENT-OBLIGATION
Intent-Preserved: directed work survives the loss of every agent, terminal, TUI, GUI, and replaceable supervisor process
Transformation: a coordination message gains an append-only obligation journal with nominal lifecycle states, generation-scoped consumption and exclusive-claim leases, explicit interruption and recovery, and evidence-bound completion
Types-Changed: DurableObligation, ConsumedObligation, ExclusiveWorkClaim, InterruptedObligation, RecoverableObligation, CompletedObligation, HostObligationTransitionReceipt
Effects-Changed: LoomObligationHostTrust admits only replayed host transitions to native frame 9007
IR-Changed: none
Claims-Introduced: one reduced journal state owns at most one current consumer or claim; an expired consumer can be fenced and recovered; an expired or interrupted claim cannot renew or complete; recovery changes generation and claim identity; completion requires nonzero canonical SHA-256 outcome and evidence digests; unclosed journals remain enumerable after total process loss
Claims-Forbidden: exactly-once side effects, replicated storage, partition tolerance, distributed consensus, Byzantine durability, semantic correctness of the evidence content, or recovery after loss of the obligation storage itself
Assumptions: Unix lock and rename semantics hold; fsync reports honestly; SHA-256 collision resistance holds; forward wall-clock skew is bounded relative to lease TTLs; one filesystem authority serializes the journal; the OCaml host replays the complete hash chain before invoking Sounio
Proof-Obligation: no two live generations own the same obligation; no completion exists without evidence; every non-completed obligation reappears after all Loom processes restart
Evidence-Run: scripts/ci/loom_obligation_typestate_gate.sh; scripts/ci/sounio_loom_obligation_adapter_selftest.sh; scripts/ci/sounio_loom_obligation_selftest.sh; scripts/ci/sounio_loom_obligation_crash_matrix_selftest.sh
Evidence-Causal: tools/loom/evidence/obligation-v1-20260824/prereg.json; tools/loom/evidence/obligation-v1-20260824/outcome.json
Evidence-Receipt: tools/loom/evidence/obligation-v1-20260824/receipt.txt
Fallback-Path: existing coordination messages, ACKs, and wake receipts remain readable and unchanged
Legacy-Kept: yes; obligations are additive and do not reinterpret transport delivery as work completion
Distinctions-Preserved: message delivery != obligation consumption; live presence != exclusive claim; ACK != completion; outcome digest != evidence digest; transport wake != execution receipt
Distinctions-Erased: none
```

## Canonical States

| Code | State | Meaning |
|---:|---|---|
| 1 | Durable | The message digest is retained as work not yet consumed. |
| 2 | Consumed | One verified process generation has accepted responsibility under an expiring lease. |
| 3 | Claimed | One actor, lane, generation, claim token, and deadline own execution. |
| 4 | Interrupted | The prior claim is closed and cannot complete. |
| 5 | Recoverable | A distinct verified generation may acquire a new claim. |
| 6 | Completed | Outcome and evidence digests are permanently bound to the claim. |

Transitions are `open`, `consume`, `claim`, `renew`, `interrupt`, `recover`, and
`complete`. Frame `9007` binds transition kind, adjacent states, obligation,
actor, generation, claim, deadline, message digest, outcome digest, and evidence
digest. The OCaml runtime may not append an event until the native Sounio adapter
accepts the corresponding frame.

## Causal Boundary

The preregistered treatment repeats a valid completion frame with a zero
evidence digest and requires native refusal. The sabotage control changes only
`completion_evidence_is_bound` to unconditional acceptance and repeats the exact
same bytes. This establishes only that the named rule causes this bounded
refusal; it is not a novelty, priority, distributed-systems, or broad
correctness claim.
